-A whole program, such as a migration across many packages, has no playbook of its own. `/poteto-mode` routes large or cross-cutting work to [`/figure-it-out`](../../skills/figure-it-out/SKILL.md), which designs one rigorous run for it:
+[Orchestrate](../../skills/poteto-mode/playbooks/orchestrate.md) is for a program that outlives any single agent: multi-day, many stacked PRs, fleets of subagents under one standing coordinator chat. The coordinator decides which agent does each piece of work, checks what each one produces, and never writes code itself. Large or cross-cutting work that one run can finish still routes to [`/figure-it-out`](../../skills/figure-it-out/SKILL.md), which designs one rigorous run. If one agent could finish the work in a session, the playbook itself routes you back to the overnight contract above:
 
